From: Colin Whittaker <colin.whittaker@adtran.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: keep the noise average on the operating channel

mt7915 and mt7996 restart their noise average at each channel set,
and the next update seeds it from one IPI histogram reading. After a
scan or an off-channel visit, the phy sets the operating channel
again, and its channel state still holds the noise floor. The
restart then makes the noise jump to one reading and settle again.
If the readings have no counts, the driver reports no noise until an
update reads counts.

When the phy sets the operating channel, continue the average from
the noise floor that the channel state holds. After a CSA or a
channel context change, that is the noise floor that the channel
state saved for the new channel. An off-channel set, or a channel
with no saved noise floor, still restarts the average.

Signed-off-by: Colin Whittaker <colin.whittaker@adtran.com>
---
 mt7915/main.c |    8 +++++++-
 mt7996/main.c |    8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -680,7 +680,13 @@ int mt7996_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	mt7996_mac_cca_stats_reset(phy);
 
 	mt7996_mac_reset_counters(phy);
-	phy->noise = 0;
+	/* continue the noise average of the operating channel instead of
+	 * starting it again from a single IPI histogram reading
+	 */
+	if (mphy->offchannel)
+		phy->noise = 0;
+	else
+		phy->noise = -mphy->chan_state->noise << 4;
 	if (!mphy->offchannel)
 		mt7996_mac_update_beacons(phy);
 
--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -368,7 +368,13 @@ int mt7915_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	mt7915_mac_cca_stats_reset(phy);
 
 	mt7915_mac_reset_counters(phy);
-	phy->noise = 0;
+	/* continue the noise average of the operating channel instead of
+	 * starting it again from a single IPI histogram reading
+	 */
+	if (mphy->offchannel)
+		phy->noise = 0;
+	else
+		phy->noise = -mphy->chan_state->noise << 4;
 
 out:
 	if (!mt76_testmode_enabled(phy->mt76))
